Shaded artifact
---------------

target/agentic-flink-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT-uber.jar (the root pom.xml, maven-shade-plugin,
   classifier `uber`). The main artifact agentic-flink-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar is thin and
   bundles nothing. The uber jar packs every compile-scope dependency of the Flink
   framework module, including the optional ones, together with their transitive closure.
   The shade configuration excludes org.apache.flink:flink-shaded-force-shading,
   com.google.code.findbugs:jsr305, org.slf4j:* and org.apache.logging.log4j:* (logging
   is provided by the Flink distribution at run time) and strips signature files.

Direct third-party components bundled by the uber jar
-----------------------------------------------------

The list below is the set of direct compile-scope dependencies of the root pom.xml at the
versions resolved by `./mvnw dependency:list -DexcludeTransitive=true -DincludeScope=runtime`,
with the license each project declares in its published POM. Components marked (optional)
are optional dependencies of the framework that the shade plugin nevertheless bundles.

Apache License, Version 2.0:
- Apache Flink CEP (org.apache.flink:flink-cep 2.2.1)
- Apache Flink Kafka connector (org.apache.flink:flink-connector-kafka 5.0.0-2.2)
- Apache Kafka client (org.apache.kafka:kafka-clients 4.1.2)
- LangChain4j and its Ollama and OpenAI modules (dev.langchain4j:* 1.23.0) (optional)
- Jackson databind, YAML dataformat and parameter-names module
  (com.fasterxml.jackson.*:* 2.22.4)

BSD 2-Clause License:
- PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (org.postgresql:postgresql 42.7.14)

Transitive components
---------------------

The transitive closure of the components above is also bundled. Their license texts and notices are carried inside the jar under
META-INF/ (META-INF/LICENSE*, META-INF/NOTICE*, META-INF/licenses/ and
META-INF/license/) because the shade plugin keeps those resources. Run
`unzip -l target/agentic-flink-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT-uber.jar | grep META-INF/maven/` for the
complete list of bundled Maven coordinates in a given build.

The other modules of the reactor (ports/jagentic-core, agentic-pekko) build thin jars and
bundle no third-party code.

The Python distributions (pyagentic, agentic-pipeline) bundle no third-party code.
